IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-fixtures`
IMPORT `ucta-schedules`

-- Tests for ucta-schedules.l4 (First and Second Schedules).  Every expected value is written
-- from the text of the Schedule, not from what the code computes.

§ `First Schedule para 1 - sections 2 to 4 do not extend to`

-- para 1(a): insurance.  Text: "Sections 2 to 4 do not extend to - (a) any contract of insurance".
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `Insurance, including a contract to pay an annuity on human life` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 1(b): land.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `The creation, transfer or termination of an interest in land` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 1(c): intellectual property.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `The creation, transfer or termination of a right or interest in intellectual property` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 1(d): company.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `The formation or dissolution of a company, or its constitution or the rights or obligations of its corporators or members` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- para 1(e): securities.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `The creation or transfer of securities, or of a right or interest in securities` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A contract that relates to none of (a) to (e): para 1 does not speak.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `None of these` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Employment is dealt with in para 4, not para 1.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` Employment EQUALS NOTHING
-- Marine salvage is dealt with in para 2, not para 1.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 sections 2 to 4 extend to the contract` `Marine salvage or towage` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `First Schedule para 2 - marine salvage, charterparty, carriage of goods by ship`

-- para 2 first sentence: "Section 2(1) extends to - (a) any contract of marine salvage or towage; (b) any charterparty ...; and (c) any contract for the carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft".
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 section 2(1) extends to the contract` `Marine salvage or towage` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 section 2(1) extends to the contract` `A charterparty of a ship or hovercraft` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 section 2(1) extends to the contract` `The carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another contract: para 2 does not say.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 section 2(1) extends to the contract` `None of these` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 section 2(1) extends to the contract` Employment EQUALS NOTHING

-- para 2 second part: "but subject to this, sections 2 to 4 and 7 do not extend to any such contract except in favour of a person dealing as consumer".
-- Not in favour of a consumer: the text says no.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` `Marine salvage or towage` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` `A charterparty of a ship or hovercraft` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` `The carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In favour of a consumer: the exception is met; the paragraph grants nothing (QA).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` `Marine salvage or towage` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` `The carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A contract that is not one of the three: the bar is on "any such contract" only.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 sections 2 to 4 and 7, subject to section 2(1), extend to the contract` `None of these` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `First Schedule para 3 - carriage of goods by ship or hovercraft over part of the journey`

-- (a) the contract specifies ship or hovercraft as the means over part of the journey; the term operates for that carriage; not in favour of a consumer.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) the contract makes no provision as to the means of carriage and does not exclude that means.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "except in favour of a person dealing as consumer": the exception is met (QA).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The goods are not carried by ship or hovercraft: "Where goods are carried by ship or hovercraft" is not met.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Carried by ship, but neither (a) nor (b): the contract specifies another means and excludes ship.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The term does not operate for the carriage by ship.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 sections 2(2), 3 and 4 extend to the contract as it operates for the carriage of the goods by ship or hovercraft` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `First Schedule para 4 - contract of employment`

-- "Subsections (1) and (2) of section 2 do not extend to a contract of employment, except in favour of the employee."
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 4 section 2(1) and (2) extend to the contract` Employment FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In favour of the employee: the exception is met (QA).
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 4 section 2(1) and (2) extend to the contract` Employment TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a contract of employment.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 4 section 2(1) and (2) extend to the contract` `None of these` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Second Schedule - guidelines`

-- The Schedule lists five matters, (a) to (e).
#ASSERT count (`sch 2 the guidelines`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `sch 2 the paragraph that states the guideline` `Bargaining positions and alternative means of meeting the customer's requirements` EQUALS "(a)"
#ASSERT `sch 2 the paragraph that states the guideline` `Inducement, or an opportunity to contract elsewhere without a similar term` EQUALS "(b)"
#ASSERT `sch 2 the paragraph that states the guideline` `Whether the customer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the term` EQUALS "(c)"
#ASSERT `sch 2 the paragraph that states the guideline` `Whether compliance with a condition was practicable` EQUALS "(d)"
#ASSERT `sch 2 the paragraph that states the guideline` `Whether the goods were made, processed or adapted to the customer's special order` EQUALS "(e)"
-- "any of the following which appear to be relevant": a relevant matter is one to have regard to; an irrelevant one is not.
#ASSERT `sch 2 regard is to be had in particular to the guideline` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 regard is to be had in particular to the guideline` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Whether it appears relevant is the court's judgment: not given, so not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 2 regard is to be had in particular to the guideline` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Schedule is for sections 6(3) and 7(3) and (4) only: for another section it is silent.
#ASSERT `sch 2 regard is to be had in particular to the guideline` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- First Schedule para 1(d)(i): "a company (which means any body corporate or unincorporated association and includes a partnership)".
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(d)(i) the entity is a company` `A body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(d)(i) the entity is a company` `An unincorporated association` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(d)(i) the entity is a company` `A partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1(d)(i) the entity is a company` `Something else` EQUALS JUST FALSE
